---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="Statecraft: Israel Content System | Jeremy Hoover"
  description="My 20 merged contributions to an open-source strategy game about Israel: historical research, contributor guidance, AI skills, UX writing standards, and shipped UI copy."
>
  <article class="section case-study case-study--violet">
    <header class="case-hero">
      <div class="container case-hero__grid">
        <div class="case-hero__main">
        <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="back"><span class="back-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Back to selected projects</span></a>
        <h1>Research, writing rules, and UI copy for a history game</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I have a background in history, so I started contributing to Statecraft: Israel, an open-source strategy game. I researched the history with sources, turned it into game data, wrote guidance and AI skills for other contributors, and rewrote player-facing copy. So far that's 20 merged pull requests.
        </p>

        <div class="outcomes-strip" aria-label="Project outcomes">
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">20 PRs</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Merged into the project</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">8 studies</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Historical research and source checks</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">4 skills</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">For research, writing, UX copy, and video scripts</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="glance-card" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
          <h2 id="glance-title">At a glance</h2>
          <dl class="glance">
              <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Contributor: historical research, writing guidance, and UX writing</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Contribution</dt><dd>I found the gaps, proposed fixes in public issues, and wrote 20 merged PRs</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>Contributor guidance, AI skills, research, game data, UI copy, localization guidance, and release notes</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Collaboration</dt><dd>The project owner, maintainers, and other contributors</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Timeframe</dt><dd>October 2026 to now</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Public issues, PRs, reviews, tests, and contributor credit</dd></div>
            </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="case-body">
      <div class="container case-shell">
        <aside class="disclosure" aria-label="Project disclosure">
          <strong>My role</strong>
          <p>Eyal Golan created Statecraft: Israel. I don't own the game. This page only covers my own public issues and merged contributions. The repo uses different licenses for code, content, docs, and assets.</p>
        </aside>

        <nav class="case-toc" aria-label="Statecraft: Israel case study sections">
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#challenge">The problem</a></li>
            <li><a href="#foundation">Contributor guidance</a></li>
            <li><a href="#research">Research</a></li>
            <li><a href="#experience">UI copy</a></li>
            <li><a href="#evidence">See the work</a></li>
            <li><a href="#reflection">What I learned</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>

        <section id="challenge" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>A game where every claim needs a source</h2>
          <p>Statecraft: Israel is a turn-based strategy game about running the country starting in 1948. It's a simulation built on real people, events, places, and political decisions. Historical claims need sources. Sensitive events need care. And the UI has to explain unfamiliar systems without dumbing down the history.</p>
          <p>The repo was moving fast: game design, Unity code, historical content, English and Hebrew, and public releases. The problem was bigger than any one string. Contributors and AI agents needed a shared way to research, write, check, and talk about the game.</p>
          <p>My history background helped. I know how to go from archives and official sources to conflicting accounts and open questions, and then decide what the game can actually say.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="gameplay-figure">
          <img src={`${base}/images/case-studies/statecraft-israel.jpg`} alt="Statecraft: Israel gameplay showing the 1948 map, city labels, resource indicators, and the Tel Aviv city-management panel" width="1600" height="900" />
          <figcaption>
            <strong>The game.</strong> The map, cities, resources, and player guidance. Screenshot from the Statecraft: Israel repo, used under its asset license.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="foundation" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>Contributor guidance first</h2>
          <p>My first big contribution didn't add anything to the game. It made the repo easier to contribute to. I added agent guidance, a writing guide, instructions for specific AI tools, reusable skills, templates, and validation scripts.</p>
          <p>That made everything after it repeatable. Nobody has to figure out sourcing, voice, or project context again in every PR. Contributors and AI agents start from the same rules and the same trusted sources.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="system-figure" aria-labelledby="system-caption">
          <div class="system-grid" role="img" aria-label="Four layers of the contribution system: repository guidance, reusable skills, validation, and product delivery">
            <div><span>01</span><strong>Guidance</strong><small>Repo rules, writing standards, and which sources to trust</small></div>
            <div><span>02</span><strong>Skills</strong><small>Historical content, writing voice, UX writing, and video scripts</small></div>
            <div><span>03</span><strong>Validation</strong><small>Templates, checkers, tests, and flagging what's uncertain</small></div>
            <div><span>04</span><strong>Delivery</strong><small>Research, game data, UI copy, and release notes</small></div>
          </div>
          <figcaption id="system-caption">
            <strong>Rules that get used.</strong> The guidance feeds the skills, and both feed the work players actually see.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="research" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>From research to game data</h2>
          <p>I wrote public research on the New Economic Policy, the Knesset vote on talks with Germany, the 1955 election, the 1948 war, the road to Suez, and the Sinai Campaign. I also checked the sources behind the quotes used in the trailer.</p>
          <p>The notes don't just list facts. They separate what's verified, what's a lead, where sources disagree, and what's still unknown. So you can see the uncertainty before anything turns into game data or copy.</p>
          <p>Then I put the research into the game: Third Knesset and 1955 election data, with source references and tests that check the new records fit the simulation.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="system-figure" aria-labelledby="pipeline-caption">
          <ol class="research-flow">
            <li><span>1</span><strong>Question</strong><small>What's missing, historically or in the game</small></li>
            <li><span>2</span><strong>Sources</strong><small>Read, compare, and record evidence</small></li>
            <li><span>3</span><strong>Research note</strong><small>Separate facts, conflicts, and gaps</small></li>
            <li><span>4</span><strong>Game content</strong><small>Turn reviewed material into game data</small></li>
            <li><span>5</span><strong>Player experience</strong><small>Explain choices and what happens next</small></li>
          </ol>
          <figcaption id="pipeline-caption">
            <strong>Sources first.</strong> Nothing reaches the game until it's clear how solid the evidence is.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="experience" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>Making the game easier to understand</h2>
          <p>Before writing any standards, I audited the UI as it existed. That turned into a 49-term glossary, six shared conventions, and English and Hebrew UI-writing guidance based on the actual game, not generic style advice.</p>
          <p>Then I used it in shipped UI changes. The save warnings now say what changed and what to do next. The How to play content explains unfamiliar training terms, ties facilities to outcomes, and says when worker changes take effect. My draft Hebrew stayed marked for native review instead of being passed off as final.</p>
          <p>I also built skills for UX writing and for sourced video scripts, with templates and checks. They make good calls easier to repeat, but source review, native-speaker review, and maintainer approval still happen in the open.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="evidence" class="content-section">
          <div class="reading-column">
            <h2>See the work</h2>
            <p>Everything is public: the original proposals, review comments, revisions, tests, and merges.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof-list" aria-label="Public contribution evidence">
            <a href="https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/pulls?q=is%3Apr+author%3Ajeremydhoover-blip+is%3Amerged" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Complete record</span><strong>Review all 20 merged pull requests</strong><small>Research, systems, content, UX, and messaging ↗</small></a>
            <a href="https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/pull/134" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Foundation</span><strong>Inspect the repository guidance and skills</strong><small>Writing guide, agent instructions, templates, and checks ↗</small></a>
            <a href="https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/pull/970" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>UX system</span><strong>Read the bilingual UX guidance contribution</strong><small>Glossary, conventions, English, and Hebrew guidance ↗</small></a>
            <a href="https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/pull/1139" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Shipped UI copy</span><strong>Compare the revised save and recovery messages</strong><small>Implementation evidence, review, and before-and-after captures ↗</small></a>
            <a href="https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/pull/1140" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Player guidance</span><strong>Inspect the revised How to play content</strong><small>Desktop and mobile evidence in English and Hebrew ↗</small></a>
            <a href="https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/blob/main/site/src/data/contributors.yaml" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Contributor credit</span><strong>View the project's public contributor record</strong><small>Repository-maintained attribution ↗</small></a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="reflection" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>What I learned</h2>
          <p>In an open, AI-assisted project, content design is a lot more than UI strings. Here it covered which sources to trust, how contributors work, agent instructions, checks, game data, translation, and release notes.</p>
          <p>Doing it in public also kept the lines clear. Maintainers decided what merged. Native speakers had the final say on Hebrew. Open historical questions stayed open. AI sped things up, but it was always obvious where a person still had to make the call.</p>
        </section>

        <aside class="inspect-work" aria-labelledby="inspect-title">
          <div>
            <h2 id="inspect-title">See the work and the game</h2>
            <p>The repo has my contribution history, the current game, the source rules, tests, and the roadmap.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="inspect-work__actions">
            <a href="https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel/pulls?q=is%3Apr+author%3Ajeremydhoover-blip+is%3Amerged" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn">View my pull requests<Icon name="arrow-outward" /></a>
            <a href="https://github.com/eyalgolan/statecraft-israel" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--outline">Explore the repository<Icon name="arrow-outward" /></a>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <hr class="divider" />
        <nav class="case-pagination" aria-label="Case study navigation">
          <a href={`${base}/work/fabric-cli`} class="case-pagination__link">
            <span class="case-pagination__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Previous project</span><span class="case-pagination__title">Fabric CLI AI skills</span></span>
          </a>
          <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="case-pagination__link">
            <span class="case-pagination__icon case-pagination__icon--index" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Project index</span><span class="case-pagination__title">All selected projects</span></span>
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-study { padding-top: 0; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  h1 { margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  .lede { max-width: 58ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-12); font-size: var(--size-xl); line-height: 1.6; }
  .outcome { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .outcome__num { line-height: 1.1; white-space: nowrap; }
  .outcome__label { max-width: 24ch; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); line-height: 1.5; }
  .case-shell { max-width: calc(var(--narrow) + 6rem); }
  .reading-column { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin-inline: auto; }
  .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 90px; }
  .content-section h2, .case-summary h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .content-section:not(:first-child) h2 { margin-top: var(--space-16); }
  .content-section p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }

  .disclosure { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: 0 auto var(--space-12); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--portfolio-blue-soft); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; }
  .disclosure strong { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: none; }
  .disclosure p { color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }

  .case-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); }
  .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .case-meta dt { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .case-meta dd { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  .case-toc { max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-8) auto var(--space-16); padding-block: var(--space-6); border-block: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .case-toc__label { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .case-toc ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .case-toc a { display: inline-flex; min-height: 32px; align-items: center; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 650; text-decoration: none; }
  .case-toc a:hover { color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 5px; }

  .gameplay-figure { width: min(100%, 880px); margin: var(--space-12) auto var(--space-16); }
  .system-figure { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-12) auto var(--space-16); }
  .gameplay-figure img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 18px; box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(16,26,45,0.12); }
  .gameplay-figure figcaption, .system-figure figcaption { margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); line-height: 1.55; }
  .gameplay-figure figcaption strong, .system-figure figcaption strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); }

  .system-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); }
  .system-grid div { display: flex; min-height: 145px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-6); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .system-grid span, .research-flow > li > span { display: grid; width: 1.8rem; height: 1.8rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .system-grid strong, .research-flow strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); }
  .system-grid small, .research-flow small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  .research-flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-2); margin: 0; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid #efc4b8; border-radius: 20px; background: var(--surface-tint); list-style: none; }
  .research-flow li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 165px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; }

  .proof-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); gap: var(--space-3); margin: var(--space-8) auto 0; }
  .proof-list a { display: flex; min-height: 150px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; color: var(--portfolio-ink); text-decoration: none; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .proof-list a:nth-child(2n) { border-top-color: var(--portfolio-coral); }
  .proof-list a:hover { box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(16,26,45,0.08); border-color: rgba(17,85,204,0.35); }
  .proof-list span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .proof-list strong { color: var(--portfolio-blue); line-height: 1.4; }
  .proof-list small { margin-top: auto; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.45; }

  .inspect-work { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: var(--space-8); align-items: center; width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-16) auto 0; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .inspect-work .tag { color: var(--portfolio-yellow); }
  .inspect-work h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: #fff; }
  .inspect-work p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); }
  .inspect-work__actions { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-3); min-width: 215px; }
  .inspect-work .btn { justify-content: center; text-align: center; }
  .inspect-work .btn--outline { color: #fff; border-color: var(--portfolio-yellow); }
  .divider { margin-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-8); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .research-flow { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .research-flow li { min-height: 140px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 130px; }
    .disclosure, .case-meta, .system-grid, .proof-list, .inspect-work { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .disclosure { gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc { margin-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-12); padding-block: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-6); }
    .case-toc a { min-height: 44px; }
    .research-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .research-flow li, .system-grid div, .proof-list a { min-height: auto; }
    .inspect-work__actions { min-width: 0; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .outcome:hover, .case-meta div:hover, .system-grid div:hover, .proof-list a:hover { transform: none; }
  }

  /* ---- Visual refresh ---- */
  /* stepper: numbered nodes on one line */
  .research-flow { --node: 36px; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; list-style: none; }
  .research-flow li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 0; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: transparent; box-shadow: none; text-align: center; }
  .research-flow li > span:first-child { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: grid; width: var(--node); height: var(--node); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; place-items: center; border: 3px solid #fff; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); box-shadow: var(--elev-1); color: #fff; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .research-flow li::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: calc(var(--node) / 2); left: 50%; z-index: 0; width: calc(100% + 0.75rem); height: 2px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); transform: translateY(-50%); }
  .research-flow li:last-child::after { content: none; }
  .research-flow li::before { content: none; }
  .research-flow strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.3; }
  .research-flow li > small:last-child { max-width: 18ch; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .research-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; }
    .research-flow li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--node) 1fr; column-gap: 1rem; align-items: start; text-align: left; }
    .research-flow li > span:first-child { grid-row: 1 / span 2; margin: 0; }
    .research-flow li::after { top: var(--node); left: calc(var(--node) / 2); width: 2px; height: calc(100% - var(--node) + 1.25rem); transform: translateX(-50%); }
    .research-flow li > small:last-child { max-width: none; }
  }

  /* card grid: open white cards, no outer box */
  .system-grid { padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; }
  .system-grid > div, .system-grid > li { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: #fff; box-shadow: var(--elev-1); }
  .system-grid strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); }
</style>
